# Fraktal Gateway arguments: one option or value per line.
# Production is fail-closed for writes until certificates, trust, credentials,
# and one or more --write-root values are provisioned. Environment variables
# are expanded.
#
# PLC transport — pick ONE --plc-endpoint:
#   opc.tcp://<host>:4840   TF6100 / multi-brand (uses the security profile below)
#   ads://<AmsNetId>:851    native TwinCAT ADS (needs fraktal_ads.dll beside the
#                           gateway exe + an AMS route; the OPC UA security
#                           profile/certs/credentials below are IGNORED for ADS)
--plc-endpoint
opc.tcp://127.0.0.1:4840
--port
8080
--path
/fraktal
--web-root
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Fraktal Gateway\web
# FraktalSetup writes one exact --allow-origin when its secure remote Web HMI
# option is selected. Caddy remains the LAN listener; this gateway stays on
# loopback. Example:
# --allow-origin
# https://192.168.100.126
--security-profile
production
--security-policy
http://opcfoundation.org/UA/SecurityPolicy#Basic256Sha256
--application-uri
urn:fraktal:gateway:%COMPUTERNAME%
--client-certificate
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Fraktal\Gateway\pki\own\certs\fraktal-gateway.der
--client-private-key
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Fraktal\Gateway\pki\own\private\fraktal-gateway.pem
--trust-list
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Fraktal\Gateway\pki\trusted\certs

# Optionally restrict reads/discovery to assigned Unit and standalone-data
# subtrees. With no --read-root, the upstream OPC UA/ADS identity defines the
# read surface. Repeat for every assigned root and shared topology subtree:
# --read-root
# PLC1/MAIN/PneumaticPress
# --read-root
# PLC1/GVL_PressFieldbus/Topology

# Add the published browse path for every Unit whose mailbox may be written:
# --write-root
# PLC1/MAIN/PneumaticPress

# Required by production, but never place secrets in this arguments file:
# FRAKTAL_OPCUA_USERNAME
# FRAKTAL_OPCUA_PASSWORD
# Optional: FRAKTAL_OPCUA_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD
